### PayVerse — payment-service (simulated UPI) through the gateway. Run 01-auth.http steps 1–2 first.

### My UPI IDs (the default pv…@payverse ID is created on sign-up)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/vpa/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Create a custom UPI ID (max 3)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/vpa
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "asha.verma" }

### Verify a UPI ID before paying (MOCK switch: only @payverse IDs exist)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/vpa/{{payeeVpa}}/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### My static QR (any amount)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/qr/static
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### A dynamic QR for 149.50, valid 15 minutes
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/qr/dynamic
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 149.50, "note": "Coffee", "validityMinutes": 15 }

> {% client.global.set("qrId", response.body.id); %}

### QR image (PNG)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/qr/{{qrId}}.png
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Decode a scanned payload
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/qr/decode
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "payload": "upi://pay?pa={{payeeVpa}}&am=149.50&cu=INR" }

### Collect: ask a UPI ID for money (the payer approves with their PIN)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/collect-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "payerVpa": "{{payeeVpa}}", "amount": 99.99, "note": "Snacks" }

> {% client.global.set("collectId", response.body.id); %}

### Collect requests waiting for me to pay
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/collect-requests?direction=INCOMING
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Approve (as the payer) — moves money through transaction-service
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/collect-requests/{{collectId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
X-Txn-Pin: 4826

### Reject (as the payer)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/collect-requests/{{collectId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
